# Processes

Durable business processes written as code: `defineProcess({ run: async (ctx, input) => … })`
over five primitives — `ctx.step`, `ctx.agent`, `ctx.approval`, `ctx.task`,
`ctx.wait`. Authoring guide: `api/src/processes/README.md` (read it before
writing a process). Design: `PROCESS_PLATFORM_DESIGN.md`.

## Rules

- New process = `api/src/processes/library/<id>.ts` + one line in
  `library/index.ts` + a test in `processes.test.ts`. Nothing else.
- Side effects only inside primitives; code between them re-runs on resume.
- Step names are identities (unique per call; put ids in loop names).
- Every tool has an effect: `read` / `write` / `destructive`. Destructive tools
  are refused inside `ctx.agent` — run them in `ctx.step` after `ctx.approval`.
- A process may only call tools in its `tools` envelope; tools only resolve
  connection slots they declare and the workspace bound.
- Every journal/DB write in the runtime happens inside a `driver.run()`
  callback (`runtime/context.ts` invariants) — never in replayed code.
- The engine is behind `Driver`/`ExecutionEngine` (`runtime/driver.ts`,
  `runtime/engine.ts`); Inngest specifics live only in
  `runtime/inngest-engine.ts` and `inngest/functions/process-run.ts`.
- Tests: `api/src/processes/**/*.test.ts` run in `vitest.apps.config.ts`
  (real Mongo, `LocalEngine`, scripted agents).
